      "text": "To find the length of \\(QS\\), we start by analyzing the given triangle \\(SQR\\). We know that \\(\\cos R = \\frac{4}{9}\\) and that \\(QR = 9\\). The cosine of an angle in a right triangle is given by the ratio of the adjacent side to the hypotenuse. Here, the adjacent side to \\(\\angle R\\) is \\(QS\\) and the hypotenuse is \\(QR\\). Thus, we can write:\n\n\\[\n\\cos R = \\frac{QS}{QR} = \\frac{QS}{9} = \\frac{4}{9}\n\\]\n\nBy solving for \\(QS\\), we get:\n\n\\[\nQS = 9 \\cdot \\frac{4}{9} = 4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the length of \\(QS\\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
